# Laws — STOP rules and exclusions

CLASS: LAWS · Last updated: 2026-08-26

## Universal STOP rules

- STOP before publicly disclosing a suspected vulnerability because
  coordinated disclosure protects users; follow `SECURITY.md` for the
  full reporting policy.
- STOP before bypassing a framework ownership or public-contract
  boundary because parallel implementations cause drift; follow
  `docs/framework/FRAMEWORK-GUIDE-v1.md` for the full workflow.
- STOP before implementing server-only `bizcity-llm-router` behavior
  here because this is the WordPress client repository; follow
  `CONTRIBUTING.md` for the repository boundary and contribution rules.

## Explicit exclusions

- `.git/` is repository metadata, so agents do not treat its internals
  as product context.
- `.worktrees/` and harness-managed worktree directories are execution
  infrastructure, so they are not product areas.
- `vendor/` and `node_modules/` are third-party dependency caches, so
  their generated contents are not repository knowledge.
- `dist/`, `build/`, `coverage/`, and `.cache/` are generated outputs
  or caches, so their source directories remain the authority.
- `plugins/bizcity-facebook-bot/logs/`, `error_log`, and other runtime
  logs are operational output, so they are not context sources.
- `tests/_archived/` is historical test material, so current test
  behavior is owned by the active test directories.

An unlisted directory is a gap in this layer, not an ignorable area.
# plugins/ — first-party WordPress feature plugins

Bundled plugins follow the `plugins/bizcity-<name>/` convention and the
framework's public contracts (`docs/framework/FRAMEWORK-GUIDE-v1.md`).
Sample plugins per the Twin AI agent standard also start here — see
`examples/bizcity-reference-plugin` for the public-contract fixture.

## Plugins

| Plugin | Path | What it owns |
|---|---|---|
| content creator | `plugins/bizcity-content-creator` | marketing content generation plugin |
| document | `plugins/bizcity-doc` | document generation plugin |
| Facebook bot | `plugins/bizcity-facebook-bot` | Facebook Messenger and automation integration |
| profile | `plugins/bizcity-profile` | business profile plugin and UI |
| content tool | `plugins/bizcity-tool-content` | content tool surfaces and runtime |
| image tool | `plugins/bizcity-tool-image` | image, design, profile, and QR studio integration |
| CRM | `plugins/bizcity-twin-crm` | CRM, lead pipeline, and campaign operations |
| Zalo BizCity | `plugins/bizcity-zalo-bizcity` | BizCity Zalo integration |
| Zalo bot | `plugins/bizcity-zalo-bot` | Zalo Bot API and webhook integration |
| BizCoach | `plugins/bizcoach-pro` | people-profile and collaboration analysis |
| Google tool | `plugins/bizgpt-tool-google` | Google-backed tool integration |

## What to Load

| Task shape | Load these | Skip these |
|---|---|---|
| Change one plugin | that plugin's dir only | sibling plugins |
| New plugin | this file + `examples/bizcity-reference-plugin` | plugin internals of others |
| Plugin ↔ core boundary | the plugin + `core/twin-core` contracts | UI assets |

Runtime logs under `plugins/bizcity-facebook-bot/logs/` are operational
output, not context (see `docs/laws.md`).

## Inputs / Outputs

- Input: framework services from `core/`; contracts from
  `core/twin-core`.
- Output: installable feature plugins; contract usage validated by
  `bin/validate-plugin-contract-registry.mjs`.
# examples/ — public SDK reference-plugin fixture

`examples/bizcity-reference-plugin` is the discoverable public-contract
implementation fixture: the canonical demonstration of how an external
plugin consumes the framework's public contracts.

## What to Load

| Task shape | Load these | Skip these |
|---|---|---|
| Study the plugin standard | `examples/bizcity-reference-plugin` | core internals |
| Update the fixture | the fixture + `core/twin-core` contracts | bundled `plugins/` |

## Inputs / Outputs

- Input: public contracts (`core/twin-core`) and SDKs (`packages/`).
- Output: the reference pattern new plugins in `plugins/` follow.

